CWS Proxy for Ubuntu
====================

Package: hk.ysk.cws.proxy
Command: cws-proxy
Page: http://127.0.0.1:8788

This package installs a private Node.js runtime, the proxy program, and
/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-cws-uhid.rules. It needs glibc 2.34 or newer
(Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04). That rule is the file
apps/proxy/udev/99-cws-uhid.rules from the source tree. It sets /dev/uhid
to group plugdev and mode 0660. postinst loads the uhid module and reloads
udev. If your account is not in plugdev, add it and log in again:

  sudo usermod -aG plugdev "$USER"

Virtual HID needs Linux /dev/uhid. It is not implemented on Windows.
This package does not run on Windows, and this repository does not publish
a Windows installer.

The phone link uses BlueZ. Install still succeeds when no phone is nearby.
Press Start in the local page after the phone is advertising.

Seeds are not absolutely safe. This is a simulator for interoperability
tests. Do not hold real digital assets with it. The package does not
contain a seed, a keystore, or a provisioning profile.

GitHub Release v1.1.0 does not attach this .deb. Build it from the
repository with apps/proxy/linux/build-deb.sh.
